<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuremberg Laws</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1935</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> Laws were two antisemitic laws passed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a> rally in Nuremberg on 15 September 1935. The Reich Citizenship Law limited citizenship to people of 'German or kindred blood', and the Law for the Protection of German Blood and German Honour banned marriage and sexual relations between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and other Germans. They were later extended to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Roma</a> and Black people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuremberg-laws.jpg" alt="Nuremberg Laws" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Herausgegeben vom Reichsministerium des Innern · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RGBL_I_1935_S_1145.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
